```c
#include <stdarg.h> // Required for variadic functions

int sum_all(int count, ...) {
    va_list args;
    int sum = 0;

    // Initialize va_list with the last fixed argument
    va_start(args, count);

    // Loop 'count' times to retrieve each integer argument
    for (int i = 0; i < count; i++) {
        sum += va_arg(args, int); // Retrieve as int
    }

    // Clean up the va_list
    va_end(args);

    return sum;
}
```
This example demonstrates `va_start` for initialization, a loop with `va_arg` for retrieval (specifying `int` type), and `va_end` for cleanup.
